    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract—This work presents sequential Bayesian detection",
      "bbox": [
        58.919952392578125,
        270.6787109375,
        300.0660705566406,
        283.0971374511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and estimation methods for nonlinear dynamic stochastic systems",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015167236328,
        285.6787109375,
        299.88812255859375,
        298.0971374511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "using measurements affected by three sources of uncertainty:",
      "bbox": [
        48.96014404296875,
        300.558837890625,
        300.1059875488281,
        312.9772644042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stochastic, set-theoretic and data association uncertainty. Fol-",
      "bbox": [
        48.96014404296875,
        315.558837890625,
        299.9861755371094,
        327.9772644042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lowing Mahler’s framework for information fusion, the paper",
      "bbox": [
        48.96014404296875,
        330.4389343261719,
        300.021240234375,
        342.85736083984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "develops the optimal Bayes ﬁlter for this problem in the form",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        345.4389343261719,
        299.909912109375,
        357.85736083984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the Bernoulli ﬁlter for interval measurements. Two numerical",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        360.31903076171875,
        299.97381591796875,
        372.7374572753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "implementations of the optimal ﬁlter are developed. The ﬁrst",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        375.31903076171875,
        299.9859619140625,
        387.7374572753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is the Bernoulli particle ﬁlter (PF), which turns out to require",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        390.31903076171875,
        300.1412658691406,
        402.7374572753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a large number of particles in order to achieve a satisfactory",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        405.1991271972656,
        299.9243469238281,
        417.6175537109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance. For the sake of reduction in the number of",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        420.1991271972656,
        299.9858703613281,
        432.6175537109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "particles, the paper also develops an implementation based on",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        435.0792236328125,
        299.9454650878906,
        447.4976501464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "box particles, referred to as the Bernoulli Box-PF. A box particle",
      "bbox": [
        48.96014404296875,
        450.0792236328125,
        300.0212707519531,
        462.4976501464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is a random sample that occupies a small and controllable",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        464.9593200683594,
        300.1414489746094,
        477.37774658203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rectangular region of non-zero volume in the target state space.",
      "bbox": [
        48.96015930175781,
        479.9593200683594,
        299.9618225097656,
        492.37774658203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Manipulation of boxes utilizes the methods of interval analysis.",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        494.83941650390625,
        299.9617919921875,
        507.2578430175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The two implementations are compared numerically and found",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        509.83941650390625,
        300.0661926269531,
        522.2578735351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to perform remarkably well: the target is reliably detected and",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        524.7195434570312,
        300.0645446777344,
        537.1380004882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the posterior probability density function of the target state",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        539.7195434570312,
        300.0223083496094,
        552.1380004882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is estimated accurately. The Bernoulli Box-PF, however, when",
      "bbox": [
        48.96018981933594,
        554.5991821289062,
        300.0655212402344,
        567.0176391601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "designed carefully, is computationally more efﬁcient.",
      "bbox": [
        48.960174560546875,
        569.5991821289062,
        255.32138061523438,
        582.0176391601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
