    {
      "text": "I. INTRODUCTION",
      "bbox": [
        398.64068603515625,
        269.54962158203125,
        476.2740478515625,
        282.83978271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The problem of study is sequential Bayesian detection",
      "bbox": [
        321.96099853515625,
        284.42974853515625,
        563.2225952148438,
        297.71990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and estimation of dynamic stochastic systems using measure-",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008239746094,
        296.42974853515625,
        563.2384033203125,
        309.71990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ments affected by three sources of uncertainty: stochastic,",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        308.30987548828125,
        563.1315307617188,
        321.60003662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "set-theoretic and data association uncertainty. The standard",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        320.30987548828125,
        563.22216796875,
        333.60003662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "measurements used for nonlinear ﬁltering are points, in the",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        332.30987548828125,
        563.0238647460938,
        345.60003662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "measurement space, affected by additive measurement noise of",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        344.1899719238281,
        563.1194458007812,
        357.4801330566406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a known probability density function (pdf) [1]. The traditional",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        356.1899719238281,
        563.29052734375,
        369.4801330566406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "measurement noise expresses uncertainty due to randomness,",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        368.070068359375,
        563.3715209960938,
        381.3602294921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "often referred to as statistical or stochastic uncertainty. In many",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
        380.070068359375,
        563.2222290039062,
        393.3602294921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "practical applications, however, this standard measurement",
      "bbox": [
        312.0008544921875,
